                    <history>
                        <origin><origDate calendar="#Gregorian" notBefore="1200" notAfter="1299">s.
                                xiii</origDate></origin>
                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_189">Durham,
                                Durham, Benedictine cathedral priory of St Cuthbert</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was accepted (albeit with a query) in the second
                                edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964). However, it
                                was later rejected in the Supplement (1987), at which point the
                                Durham section was completely revised by A. J. Piper. The
                                corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records
                                the following information, which was ultimately deemed
                                unsatisfactory for an attribution:</p><p>
                                <q>In s. xiv apparently at Kingsbury, Somerset. Fol. iiv <q>Lan del
                                        Encarnation noste Seigneur M. C. XCVII le ior de la Tephaine
                                        furent sor le fiertre Saint Cuthbert c &amp; vij Besanz
                                        &amp; xlv anneals</q> (s. xvi-xvii). The calendar has Durham
                                    features, but not all the features of the Durham calendar;
                                    Wormald <title>English Benedictine Kalendars after A.D.
                                        1100.</title></q></p></provenance>
                    </history>
